# What the build context must not carry. Two kinds: what the image builds for itself,
# and what would put a secret or the working record inside a layer.

# The key, and anything else a person filled in locally.
.env
*.local.json

# Built here by `python -m veritas.ingestion`, from `data/snapshots/`, which stays.
data/veritas.duckdb
data/raw/
data/interim/

# A host virtual environment for a host interpreter — `uv sync` builds the image's own.
.venv/

# The working record, the scratch directory and the history. None of it is read at
# run time, and `README.md` points a reader at the repository for all three.
.claude/
.git/
.github/
scratch/

# Test and cache artefacts.
tests/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
